From 2c0d60f7fdd36d550944f4ee16c62bedd01e5d4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:36:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the settings that the Hades texts name, by the names
 Kodi shows in each language
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A text that sends the user to a setting has to name it as the list shows it, or the name is
looked for and not found. What Kodi 22 shows: in en_gb the core strings of this tree; in Spanish
the Estuary twin of a Hades string, else Kodi's language add-on that the Piers repository serves
(mirrors.kodi.tv/addons/piers: resource.language.es_es 11.0.109, es_ar 11.0.74, es_mx 11.0.85),
else the English.

en_gb (Estuary and its core twin; the msgid of the Spanish files with it):
- 31922 / 39872: "Turn on Dolby Vision Low-Latency" named no setting; it is "Dolby Vision for
  TVs in game mode (Low-Latency)";
- 32631 / 41151: "HDR10 as Dolby Vision, measured" is "Make HDR10 videos Dolby Vision
  (measured)";
- 31712 / 39978: "the adjustment of the display's refresh rate to the video" is the setting
  'Adjust display refresh rate'.
es_es, es_ar and es_mx, the same three, and the options that the help of a setting names, as
its list shows them: "Cuando hace falta" (#39969), "Siempre directa, Siempre compuesta"
(#39967, #39968), "Conversión a BT.2020" (#39897), and "Apagado", Kodi's #351, where 31712 and
31722 said "Desactivado".
es_es also quoted Kodi's own settings otherwise than its add-on shows them: "Sincronizar
reproducción con pantalla" (#13510), "Ajustar tasa de refresco de la pantalla" (#170),
"Permitir passthrough" (#348), and Settings > System > Audio is "Ajustes > Sistema > Sonido"
(#14221).
es_ar: Kodi's es_AR add-on leaves #21460 and #39182 untranslated, so 32293 quotes them as the
list shows them: "Position on screen" and "Vertical margin".

Host tests (outside the tree): measure.py, measure.py --reasons and measure_all.py in en_gb,
es_es, es_ar and es_mx: no text wider than its label. msgidsync, maptest, pairs, po-dups,
idtable, check-text.py of the battery and the F-d texts check: no fault. A check of every quote
and path of the Hades texts, and of every option that a help names, against the names above:
none left that is not a name shown.
---
